    "title": "Recognize conversational passives",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk4-passive-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Recognize conversational passives",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "The affected participant comes first, followed by a passive marker, an expressed agent and the action. Do not confuse this with asking or allowing the first participant to act. 让 can introduce the agent of an adverse passive event; distinguish this from causative 让, where the subject asks or causes someone to act.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我的自行车叫人骑走了。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ de zìxíngchē jiào rén qí zǒu le 。",
                "meaning": "Someone rode off with my bicycle.",
                "audio": "b6a1524fa0730338e33e483d3ac8660fd6bbb7a68b7739f1fba7b0143f5fb672"
              },
              {
                "text": "这杯水让他喝完了。",
                "pinyin": "zhè bēi shuǐ ràng tā hē wán le 。",
                "meaning": "This cup of water was all drunk by him.",
                "audio": "33bae51562713ff83f25111879f2c1a7f08bb8a8bea2e834a58634d0ec6cfd63"
              },
              {
                "text": "老师让我读书。",
                "pinyin": "lǎoshī ràng wǒ dú shū 。",
                "meaning": "The teacher asks me to read.",
                "audio": "ef02794a6981207e83264a4cbfb86b9e555733e1759fbc0619a4b976b56b674e"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
